millions of people around the world  depend directly on the Seas for their  food and livelihood for their well-being  and their future seafood is fundamental  for health and nutrition but also for  jobs and welfare today many factors  threaten the sustainability of world  fisheries like over-exploitation  unsustainable practices or illegal  fishing as the largest market in value  and the largest donor of development aid  the EU is a key player in the fight  against illegal fishing supporting  marine science and promoting market  transparency central to this is  increasing the capacity of communities  to control protect and trade their local  resources sustainably but U is therefore  supporting people around the globe to  better manage their fisheries and  aquaculture securing food  reducing poverty and delivering real  growth that is sustainable and inclusive  by helping partners technically and  financially the EU enables international  changemakers to inspire others like  training mauritania Nguyen  in better fish processing techniques or  supporting people in Madagascar to  better target stock the market  much-sought-after mangrove crabs while  also protecting their habitat or  co-financing an ambitious surveillance  program around the Indian Ocean pooling  and maximizing each country's assets to  fight illegal fishing at a regional  level the EU is convinced that the  future depends on our collective ability  to learn and adapt and find  collaborative solutions to global  challenges helping to make  sustainability and help the environment  the right and the responsibility of  everyone everywhere  [Music]
 

